  "body": "Closes #1452\nClaim: cloud/i1452-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/i1452-sonnet)\n\n**Problem.** With « Bouton + » = « Pas d'icône » the reader has no reply button, so no quote-less reply path (legacy keeps « Répondre » in the « … » menu, `MessagesView.swift:5575-5600` @ `87fe0d1c`).\n\n**Cause.** LOT-186 D2 moved « Répondre » to the bottom bar and left it out of the overflow; the hidden mode was not decided. Operator decision on #1452 (2026-11-28): option 1.\n\n**Change.** `ReaderOverflow.Entry.reply`, placed right after « Rechercher »; pure `ReaderOverflow.offersReply` (hidden mode + account + answer form + no open composer); `TopicReaderView` wires it to the same `requestReply()` as the bar button. Other modes unchanged. `reply:` defaults to false so existing callers compile unchanged.\n\n**Tests** (`ReaderOverflowTests`): `replyComesRightAfterSearch`, `replyIsInTheOverflowOnlyWithoutABarButton`. Not run here (Linux, app target): they cannot compile without `Entry.reply` / `offersReply`; compile check and CI will run them.\n\n### Ledger\n\n```gap-edit\nGAP-102\nSwiftHFR final: Floating reply button with its \"Bouton +\" setting, same values; the default is « Répondre comme le forum » (`forum`) since #1016, a stored value is kept. « Répondre » is a bottom-bar button (LOT-186 D2) and is in the « … » menu, after « Rechercher », only when « Bouton + » is « Pas d'icône » (#1452), so that mode keeps a quote-less reply; legacy has it in the menu in every mode. The button stays in landscape on an iPhone (LOT-186 D4, b·operator).\nLot/Feat: #654, #1016, #1452\n```\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
