   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, af0788d8b9a195613, round 1)**\n\n**Revue adversariale (Opus 5.5) : CHANGEMENTS DEMANDÉS** — tête adb99a4\n\n1. **High**, `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/TopicReaderView.swift:403`: the 4 added lines take the file from 399 to 403 lines. CI runs `swiftlint lint --strict` (`.github/workflows/ci.yml:28`), so the `file_length` limit (400) becomes an error. I reproduced it: `swiftlint lint --strict` gives rc=2 at the head and rc=0 with the base file. Every lint run on this PR will be red. Fix: get back under 400 lines. You can put the `offersReply(...)` call on one line, or move `replySymbol` and the `offersReply` inputs into a small helper. Don't add a `swiftlint:disable` without a reason.\n2. **Medium**, `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/TopicsSettingsModel.swift:84`: the info bubble text for « Pas d'icône » still says « réponds depuis le menu d'un message (« Citer ») ». Issue #1452 points at this exact sentence as part of the problem, and #1062 requires the text to follow what the code does. After this change it is wrong: a plain reply is now possible from « … » › Répondre. Fix: reword it. Any test that pins this sentence must change with it.\n3. **Low**, `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/ReaderOverflowToolbar.swift:46-48`: the overflow « Répondre » is never disabled. The bottom-bar button is disabled under `isLoadingQuote` (`ReaderPageControls.swift:196`), and so is the legacy one (`.disabled(isLoadingQuoteTemplate)`, `MessagesView.swift` @ 87fe0d1c). If a quote fetch is running, a tap does nothing: `requestReply` returns silently on `composerSlotIsFree`. Fix: pass a busy flag and apply `.disabled`, as is already done for `filterIsBusy`.\n\nChecked and OK: the `entries(...)` default `reply: false` keeps existing call sites compiling; the `switch` over `Entry` is exhaustive; `ReplyButtonBehavior` comes from `HFRModels` (imported); `replyTarget` requires the answer form and `composer` is nil when logged out; `ReaderOverflowToolbar` is only used by `TopicReaderView`. Not built or run on Linux.\n\n**Round 1 fixes** (one commit): (1) the call moved into `TopicReaderModel.overflowReply`, `TopicReaderView.swift` back at 400 lines, `swiftlint --strict` rc=0 on the touched files; (2) bubble reworded: « Répondre » est dans le menu « … » du sujet, « Citer » dans le menu d'un message (no test pins it); (3) `ReplyItem.busy` = `isLoadingQuote`, `.disabled(reply.busy)`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
