   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, a858289b172b597bc, round 2)**\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, reviewer of #1458): APPROVE** — head ceff9f4b\n\nFindings:\n1. Detail — `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/ReaderOverflowToolbar.swift:35-41`: tests pin the order and `offersReply`, but not the wiring in `overflowReply`. Scenario: someone later passes `isLoading` instead of `isLoadingQuote`, or drops `suspendsPageInteractions`, and every test stays green. Optional fix: a test that builds the model and reads `offered` and `busy` with and without an open composer. Not blocking: the pure rule is covered.\n\nChecked against the spec (#1452, option 1): « Répondre » only for `.hidden`, with an account and an answer form (same conditions as `replySymbol`); right after « Rechercher » as legacy (`MessagesView.swift:5575-5600` @ 87fe0d1c); same `requestReply()`, disabled while a quote loads, absent under an open composer; header comment and « Pas d'icône » help text updated; `gap-edit` GAP-102 parses (`ledger.py check-body`: 1 block ok). Compiler rigour: `overflowReply` is MainActor-isolated (extension of a `@MainActor` class), the closure and its `Task` inherit it, `let` is allowed in the `@ToolbarContentBuilder`, `reply: Bool = false` keeps existing call sites compiling. `swiftlint lint --strict` on the 4 touched files: 0 violations. Tests not run (app target, Linux).\n\nFinding 1 is optional and not taken: the model's wiring needs a full `TopicReaderModel` fixture, and the Compile check plus the owed device check cover it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
